category":"Met","severity":"Minor","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Coastal Flood Advisory","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS San Francisco CA","headline":"Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 17 at 2:27PM PST until November 19 at 10:00AM PST by NWS San Francisco CA","description":"* WHAT...Up to 1.3 ft of inundation above ground level is\npossible in low-lying areas near shorelines and tidal\nwaterways.\n\n* WHERE...Bayshore locations along the San Franciso Bay and San\nPablo Bay.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 AM Wednesday to 10 AM PST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High tides will result in flooding of low-lying\ninfrastructure, isolated road closures, and coastal erosion.\nRising tides will bring water and waves farther up the beach\nthan normal, restricting escape from beaches and coastal areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...At the San Francisco tidal gauge, high tide\nis expected to be 1.3 ft above normal (7.1 ft MLLW) at 6:45 AM\nWednesday and 1.2 ft above normal (7.0 ft MLLW) at 7:15 AM\nThursday. These predictions include up to 1.3 ft of surge that\nwill enhance the astronomical tide and flooding threat. High\ntide varies up to 90 minutes earlier or later along the Pacific\nCoast and through the San Francisco Bay, respectively.","instruction":"If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.","response":"Monitor","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["CFWMTR"],"WMOidentifier":["WHUS46 KMTR 172227"],"NWSheadline":["COASTAL FLOOD ADVISORY REMAINS IN EFFECT FROM 5 AM WEDNESDAY TO 10 AM PST THURSDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMTR.CF.Y.0017.261118T1300Z-261119T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-19T10:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["NWS"],"NationalWeatherService":["CFY"]}}