High Surf Advisory, from 4 PM Wednesday to\n4 PM PST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Large breaking waves can overpower swimmers, pulling\npeople into the sea from beaches, jetties, and rocks resulting\nin significant physical injury and increasing the risk of\ndrowning. Waves can sweep across the shoreline without warning,\npulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties, and rocks.","instruction":"Swimmers should remain out of the water due to dangerous surf\nconditions.\n\nStay off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside\ninfrastructure. Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous surf\nand NEVER turn your back on the ocean. Monitor local weather,\nsurf and tide forecasts at www.weather.gov/mtr.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["CFWMTR"],"WMOidentifier":["WHUS46 KMTR 172227"],"NWSheadline":["BEACH HAZARDS STATEMENT REMAINS IN EFFECT THROUGH WEDNESDAY AFTERNOON... ...HIGH SURF ADVISORY REMAINS IN EFFECT FROM 4 PM WEDNESDAY TO 4 PM PST THURSDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMTR.SU.Y.0005.261119T0000Z-261120T0000Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-19T16:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["NWS"],"NationalWeatherService":["SUY"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f5226d77d27eb424ae4b1298bfe533fde9c99bd9.003.2","type":"Feature","geometry":null,"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f5226d77d27eb424ae4b1298bfe533fde9c99bd9.003.2","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f5226d77d27eb424ae4b1298bfe533fde9c99bd9.003.2","areaDesc":"Coastal North Bay Including Point Reyes National Seashore; San Francisco Peninsula Coast; Northern Monterey Bay; Southern Monterey Bay and Big Sur Coast","geocode":{"SAME":["006041","006097","006081","006087","006053"],"UGC":["CAZ505","CAZ509","CAZ529","CAZ530"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/CAZ505","https:/